title: v5.37.11 — paradigm_portal_add_gate silent-no-op hotfix
summary: 'Field-reported bug: paradigm_portal_add_gate returned perfect-looking success JSON for 11 calls in another project, but gates: [] stayed empty. Root cause: portal-writer.ts guard `if (!data.gates) data.gates = {}` fails when gates is `[]` (truthy Array); subsequent property assignment on the Array is silently dropped by js-yaml.dump; handler constructs success response from input id without reading back. Compounded by v2 scaffold emitting gates: [] / routes: [] by default. Team triaged (reviewer found root cause, Explore mapped blast radius across 6 sibling handlers, Jinx designed prevention strategy). Builder shipped 3-part hotfix + first tests/ directory in paradigm-mcp with 8 regression tests. Reviewer approved-with-changes (none blocking). Residual silent-no-op risk in handleAddComponent/Link/Remove/Rename tracked as follow-up.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#portal-writer'
  - '#purpose-portal'
  - '#shift-files'
