  - packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/portal-writer.ts
  - packages/paradigm-mcp/src/tools/purpose-portal.ts
  - packages/paradigm-mcp/vitest.config.ts
  - packages/paradigm/src/commands/shift-files.ts
  - CHANGELOG.md
decisions:
  - id: d1
    decision: Fix the guard pattern in-place rather than introduce writeAndConfirm wrapper
    rationale: Hotfix scope discipline — wrapper is systemic refactor that deserves its own release. Point patch + read-back verification gets shipping users unblocked today.
  - id: d2
    decision: Apply Array→{} defense to purpose-portal handlers too, not just portal-writer
    rationale: Reviewer's blast-radius mapping showed the same guard pattern in handleAddGate/Signal/State/Aspect/Flow. Symmetric fix is ~65 LOC and eliminates the entire family of the bug, not just the reported instance.
  - id: d3
    decision: 'Scaffold emits gates: {} / routes: {} going forward; existing projects self-heal on first mutation'
    rationale: Writer normalizes Array→{} on read, so no explicit migration needed. Avoids writing a migration script for a trivially idempotent fix.
  - id: d4
    decision: Committed team audit trail (reviews/2026-04-20-*.md) alongside the code
    rationale: Preserves the triage record so future bug hunts can compare against this baseline, same pattern as the README audit commit.
learnings:
  - 'Fake success is worse than any explicit error — field agent ran 11 calls trusting the response, only caught by the stop hook noticing drift at session end. Rule: when designing any schema-mutating MCP tool, the success response must be derived from the post-write file read, not from the input payload.'
  - 'The Array vs. Object shape ambiguity in YAML scaffolds bites hard when guards use truthy checks. `if (!x)` is wrong when x can be a truthy empty container. Paradigm convention going forward: use type-aware normalization (`if (!x || Array.isArray(x)) x = {}`) whenever mutating a v2 schema field.'
  - paradigm-mcp had zero tests in packages/paradigm-mcp/tests/ before this bug. Systemic gap — the tool-registry.test.ts and notebook-loader.test.ts are under src/ but the mutation tool family had nothing. First test file now exists as precedent.
  - js-yaml silently drops named properties on Array instances during dump. Not our code's fault — but our code shouldn't assign to Arrays as if they were Objects. Future shared writer helpers must normalize shape before mutation.
